<Docs title="Overview">
  <h1>Life</h1>
  <p class="lead">Life is a protocol for agent-legible repos. A <code>.life</code> file in any directory tells an agent what that directory is, what it needs, what it provides, and which commands are safe to run. A repo with a <code>.life</code> at root is <strong>a .life</strong> — a repo that remembers, acts, and evolves.</p>

  <p>These pages are the on-ramp: how to get a repo running, and what this genepool promises the repos that depend on it. <strong>Everything conceptual and everything normative is <a href="/book">the Book of Life</a></strong> — the canon, in {size}, rendered from the <code>life-guide</code> and <code>laws</code> genes every <code>.life</code> already carries. That is deliberate: the reference and the thing it describes ship as one artifact, so they cannot drift apart. A page here that explained the protocol would be a second copy, and the second copy is always the one that goes stale.</p>

